Return a single JSON object with these fields:

{
  "jobName": "string — JOB card name",
  "class": "string — JOB CLASS parameter, or empty",
  "msgclass": "string — JOB MSGCLASS parameter, or empty",
  "steps": [
    {
      "stepName": "string — step name from // label",
      "pgm": "string — PGM= value on EXEC card, or empty if PROC step",
      "proc": "string — PROC name if EXEC procname (no PGM=), else empty",
      "cond": "string — step COND parameter, or empty",
      "ddCards": [
        {
          "ddName": "string — DD name (e.g., CUSTFILE, SYSUT1)",
          "dsname": "string — dataset name from DSN= or DSNAME=",
          "disp": "string — full DISP parameter (e.g., (OLD), (NEW,CATLG,DELETE), SHR)",
          "isInput": true,
          "isOutput": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- pgm = PGM= value on EXEC card; proc = PROC name if EXEC procname (no PGM= keyword)
- DD DISP=(OLD) or DISP=SHR -> isInput=true, isOutput=false
- DD DISP=(NEW,CATLG) or DISP=MOD -> isInput=false, isOutput=true
- DD DISP=(OLD,DELETE) -> isInput=true, isOutput=true
- Skip system DDs (SYSPRINT, SYSOUT, SYSUDUMP, CEEDUMP, SYSIN with * data) unless they have meaningful DSNAMEs
- For PROC steps, extract DD overrides as ddCards
- For concatenated DDs (multiple DD statements for same DD name), use the first DSN and note concatenation in disp
- If a step has no DD cards, return an empty ddCards array
- Return ONLY the JSON object, no markdown fences, no explanation